        confidential nodes
    containerdConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigContainerdConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        containerd config
    diskSizeGb : float, default is Undefined, optional
        Size of the disk attached to each node, specified
        in GB. The smallest allowed disk size is 10GB. Defaults to 100GB.
    diskType : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Type of the disk attached to each node
        (e.g. 'pd-standard', 'pd-balanced' or 'pd-ssd'). If unspecified, the default disk type is 'pd-balanced'
    enableConfidentialStorage : bool, default is Undefined, optional
        Enabling Confidential Storage will create boot disk with confidential mode. It is disabled by default.
    ephemeralStorageLocalSsdConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigEphemeralStorageLocalSsdConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        ephemeral storage local ssd config
    fastSocket : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigFastSocket, default is Undefined, optional
        fast socket
    flexStart : bool, default is Undefined, optional
        Enables Flex Start provisioning model for the node pool.
    gcfsConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigGcfsConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        gcfs config
    guestAccelerator : [ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigGuestAcceleratorItems0], default is Undefined, optional
        List of the type and count of accelerator cards attached to the instance.
        Structure documented below.
        Note: As of 6.0.0, argument syntax
        is no longer supported for this field in favor of block syntax.
        To dynamically set a list of guest accelerators, use dynamic blocks.
        To set an empty list, use a single guest_accelerator block with count = 0.
    gvnic : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigGvnic, default is Undefined, optional
        gvnic
    hostMaintenancePolicy : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigHostMaintenancePolicy, default is Undefined, optional
        host maintenance policy
    imageType : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The image type to use for this node. Note that changing the image type
        will delete and recreate all nodes in the node pool.
    kubeletConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigKubeletConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        kubelet config
    labels : {str:str}, default is Undefined, optional
        The Kubernetes labels (key/value pairs) to be applied to each node. The kubernetes.io/ and k8s.io/ prefixes are
        reserved by Kubernetes Core components and cannot be specified.
    linuxNodeConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigLinuxNodeConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        linux node config
    localNvmeSsdBlockConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigLocalNvmeSsdBlockConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        local nvme ssd block config
    localSsdCount : float, default is Undefined, optional
        The amount of local SSD disks that will be
        attached to each cluster node. Defaults to 0.
    localSsdEncryptionMode : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Possible Local SSD encryption modes:
        Accepted values are:
    loggingVariant : str, default is Undefined, optional
        wide default value. Valid values include DEFAULT and MAX_THROUGHPUT. See Increasing logging agent throughput for more information.
    machineType : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The name of a Google Compute Engine machine type.
        Defaults to e2-medium. To create a custom machine type, value should be set as specified
        here.
    maxRunDuration : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The runtime of each node in the node pool in seconds, terminated by 's'. Example: "3600s".
    metadata : {str:str}, default is Undefined, optional
        The metadata key/value pairs assigned to instances in
        the cluster. From GKE 1. To avoid this, set the
        value in your config.
    minCpuPlatform : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Minimum CPU platform to be used by this instance.
        The instance may be scheduled on the specified or newer CPU platform. Applicable
        values are the friendly names of CPU platforms, such as Intel Haswell. See the
        official documentation
        for more information.
    nodeGroup : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Setting this field will assign instances of this pool to run on the specified node group. This is useful for running workloads on sole tenant nodes.
    oauthScopes : [str], default is Undefined, optional
        The set of Google API scopes to be made available
        on all of the node VMs under the "default" service account.
        Use the "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform" scope to grant access to all APIs. It is recommended that you set service_account to a non-default service account and grant IAM roles to that service account for only the resources that it needs.
    preemptible : bool, default is Undefined, optional
        A boolean that represents whether or not the underlying node VMs
        are preemptible. See the official documentation
        for more information. Defaults to false.
    reservationAffinity : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigReservationAffinity, default is Undefined, optional
        reservation affinity
    resourceLabels : {str:str}, default is Undefined, optional
        The GCP labels (key/value pairs) to be applied to each node. Refer here
        for how these labels are applied to clusters, node pools and nodes.
    resourceManagerTags : {str:str}, default is Undefined, optional
        A map of resource manager tag keys and values to be attached to the nodes for managing Compute Engine firewalls using Network Firewall Policies. Tags must be according to specifications found here. A maximum of 5 tag key-value pairs can be specified. Existing tags will be replaced with new values. Tags must be in one of the following formats ([KEY]=[VALUE]) 1. tagKeys/{tag_key_id}=tagValues/{tag_value_id} 2. {org_id}/{tag_key_name}={tag_value_name} 3. {project_id}/{tag_key_name}={tag_value_name}.
    secondaryBootDisks : [ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigSecondaryBootDisksItems0], default is Undefined, optional
        Parameters for secondary boot disks to preload container images and data on new nodes. Structure is documented below. gcfs_config must be enabled=true for this feature to work. min_master_version must also be set to use GKE 1.28.3-gke.106700 or later versions.
    serviceAccount : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The service account to be used by the Node VMs.
        If not specified, the "default" service account is used.
    serviceAccountRef : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigServiceAccountRef, default is Undefined, optional
        service account ref
    serviceAccountSelector : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigServiceAccountSelector, default is Undefined, optional
        service account selector
    shieldedInstanceConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigShieldedInstanceConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        shielded instance config
    soleTenantConfig : ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigSoleTenantConfig, default is Undefined, optional
        sole tenant config
    spot : bool, default is Undefined, optional
        A boolean that represents whether the underlying node VMs are spot.
        See the official documentation
        for more information. Defaults to false.
    storagePools : [str], default is Undefined, optional
        The list of Storage Pools where boot disks are provisioned.
    tags : [str], default is Undefined, optional
        The list of instance tags applied to all nodes. Tags are used to identify
        valid sources or targets for network firewalls.
    taint : [ContainerGcpmUpboundIoV1beta1ClusterSpecForProviderNodeConfigTaintItems0], default is Undefined, optional
